 A vs exp 3.615 A (+0.7%, typical of PBE). Cu cohesive energy 3.50 eV vs exp 3.49 eV (textbook, Kittel). O2 binding 6.28 eV and bond 1.235 A, vs exp De ~5.2 eV: this is PBE-like overbinding of about 1.1 eV per O2, about 0.5 eV per O. The 1/4 ML fcc value (-4.90 eV) and fcc-hcp ordering match a PBE/VASP preprint found by web search (arXiv:2505.12914, as summarised by the search tool: fcc -5.00, hcp -4.905 eV vs gas-phase O). I did not read that paper myself, so treat it as a secondary check. UNCERTAINTY (0.5 eV, approximate): model error vs PBE about 0.1-0.15 eV; finite size/slab under 0.07 eV; atomic reference ambiguity up to about 0.5 eV. Combining E_ads(1/2 O2) = -1.69 eV with the experimental O2 De (about 5.21 eV) gives about -4.30 eV. So -4.84 eV is a PBE-level number; an experiment-scale estimate is about 0.5 eV weaker. No ZPE or thermal corrections are included; O ZPE on hollow sites is about 0.05-0.1 eV.\"}\nEOF\n./board post property_result @/work/scripts/result.json --parent ff1090ba-e6d0-4bad-91a5-5499964be846"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":31474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1039,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af5c6b74-7303-4519-9ec9-ea0c84897381","uuid":"17b171a4-0f06-4c91-9525-80290525580a","timestamp":"2026-11-01T03:01:42.317Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTnowGtvgHHsnrjBGUJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AGUFGYXgDGnvEgRLReMyLN":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/scripts/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"O on Cu(111)\", \"family\": \"adsorbate/metal surface\", \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\", \"value\": -4.84, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.5,\